          "context": "Yes\n Evidence 2: Did Sen. Martha McSally support a plan to raise the retirement age?  Yes. "
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-67fcc48de84f::sentence-4",
          "documentId": "doc-67fcc48de84f",
          "text": "Evidence 1: Did Sen. Martha McSally support a plan to turn Medicare into a voucher program? ",
          "start": 194,
          "end": 286,
          "context": "Source URL: https://clerk.house.gov/Votes/2017557\n Evidence 1: Did Sen. Martha McSally support a plan to turn Medicare into a voucher program?  Although McSally endorsed a move to a premium-support or voucher system in 2017, she voted against her party in 2015, when she supported a motion that instructed House conferees to prevent Medicare from becoming a voucher program.\n\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-b7039c2b13f6::sentence-17",
          "documentId": "doc-b7039c2b13f6",
          "text": "I support reform such as modernizing the retirement age and indexing it to life expectancy. ",
          "start": 1270,
          "end": 1362,
          "context": "But no longer can we simply “protect” Social Security as some politicians seek to do; we must make needed reforms to “preserve” it for future generations.  I support reform such as modernizing the retirement age and indexing it to life expectancy.  I also support giving younger workers the opportunity to invest a portion of their money in optional personal accounts. "
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-b7039c2b13f6::sentence-12",
          "documentId": "doc-b7039c2b13f6",
          "text": "Is Social Security, as it now exists, survivable and would you support raising the cap on earning, raising the retirement age, reducing payments to wealthier Americans and allow younger workers to invest a portion of the Social Security into private accounts? ",
          "start": 627,
          "end": 887,
          "context": "Question 3\n Is Social Security, as it now exists, survivable and would you support raising the cap on earning, raising the retirement age, reducing payments to wealthier Americans and allow younger workers to invest a portion of the Social Security into private accounts?  What proposals would you make to ensure it is available for future generations?\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-67fcc48de84f::sentence-5",
          "documentId": "doc-67fcc48de84f",
          "text": "Although McSally endorsed a move to a premium-support or voucher system in 2017, she voted against her party in 2015, when she supported a motion that instructed House conferees to prevent Medicare from becoming a voucher program.\n\n",
          "start": 286,
          "end": 518,
          "context": "Evidence 1: Did Sen. Martha McSally support a plan to turn Medicare into a voucher program?  Although McSally endorsed a move to a premium-support or voucher system in 2017, she voted against her party in 2015, when she supported a motion that instructed House conferees to prevent Medicare from becoming a voucher program.\n\n RECOVERED SOURCE TEXT\n"
        }
      ]
    }
